From: =?UTF-8?q?=C3=98yvind=20Harboe?= <oyvind.harboe@zylin.com>
Subject: [PATCH] gpl: -dataflow_pull_weight, groups pulled toward the macros
 they feed

Rung 4 of bazel-orfs #1263, after DG-RePlAce's dataflow virtual nets:
before Nesterov placement, a walk from each macro, forward from its
outputs and backward from its inputs, through combinational cells and
up to three register stages (nets of more than 50 pins skipped, so
clock, reset and enable trees do not count) gives each group of cells
(-cluster_pull_depth's groups) an affinity to each macro: the mean over
its cells of 0.5^stage. A group keeps its four strongest macros. In
Nesterov placement every cell of a group is pulled with the group's
pull toward those macros, bounded by weight times affinity per macro and
fading with the cluster pull over -cluster_pull_iters.

rtl_macro_placer no longer models dataflow, so the walk is here. It uses
the liberty view to tell registers from combinational cells. Results are
the same at any thread count: the walk and the group centroids are
serial, in a fixed order.

Carried in bazel-orfs to measure the idea of issue #1263; not upstreamed.
Retires with 0127.
